  "uncertain": [
    "Image 1 shows a module marked 'RAK3172-SIP' and no board name; the image does not show that it is the RAK3272-SiP breakout board named in this record (image 2 is marked RAK3272-SiP).",
    "Image 2 label-to-pad mapping is inferred: the four 9-label columns (PA1 1..3V3, PC6..PB8, PB11..PA10, PA7..3V3) were assigned left-to-right to outer-left pads, J5, J6, outer-right pads. The first column is printed directly beside J5 and the fourth beside J6, so J5 = PA1 1..3V3 and J6 = PA7..3V3 is an equally possible reading.",
    "Image 2 J7/J8 mapping is inferred: the two label rows 'PB15 PA15 PC13' and 'PB5 PB4 PB3' are both printed above J7 and were assigned top-to-bottom to J7 then J8; PA8/3V3 (J7 ends) and GND/3V3 (J8 ends) are printed beside the rows. Which middle hole each label belongs to is also inferred from horizontal position.",
    "Image 1 inner hole columns and the 2x5 hole block at the bottom are unlabeled in that image and were not transcribed."
  ],
  "notes": "Image 1 is a labeled pinout of the front (J3/J4 outer headers with printed pin numbers). Image 2 is the silkscreen side marked 'RAK3272-SiP Ver .A' with designators J5-J8; its labels are printed as a 4-column, 9-row table plus two 3-label rows, not beside individual holes, and are mapped to pad columns/rows in left-to-right and top-to-bottom order. 'PA1 1' and 'PA1 2' are printed with a gap and recorded as printed. In image 1 the inner hole columns and the bottom 2x5 hole block carry no labels and are not transcribed; the SMA and u.FL antenna connectors are skipped."
